!script {{
  --/| ==========================================================================
  --/| Tutorial 17: D&D 2024 Beacon Roll Modes and Targeted Roll Bonuses
  --/|
  --/| PURPOSE
  --/| The D&D 2024 sheet has TWO different ideas that are easy to confuse:
  --/|
  --/| 1. A GLOBAL d20 roll mode for the character.
  --/| 2. Targeted Advantage, Disadvantage, or numeric modifiers supplied by rules
  --/|    such as armor, Conditions, Effects, Features, and other records.
  --/|
  --/| GLOBAL ROLL MODE
  --/| The global setting is:
  --/|
  --/| sheet->settings->rolls->mode
  --/|
  --/| Verified values are:
  --/| Automatic, Advantage, Disadvantage
  --/|
  --/| This setting is sheet-wide. It is NOT the red Advantage/Disadvantage marker
  --/| shown beside one specific skill or save.
  --/|
  --/| TARGETED ROLL OVERRIDES
  --/| Those are represented by Roll Bonus records in the rollbonuses collection.
  --/|
  --/| Important Roll Bonus fields include:
  --/| bonusCategory  = what kind of roll is affected
  --/| bonusName      = the specific roll inside that category, if any
  --/| bonusDetails   = Keep Highest, Keep Lowest, or Modifier
  --/| bonusValue     = numeric value used by Modifier records
  --/| parentID       = the Roll Bonus record's immediate parent
  --/|
  --/| Keep Highest = Advantage
  --/| Keep Lowest  = Disadvantage
  --/|
  --/| SOURCE APPLICABILITY
  --/| A Roll Bonus can exist even while its source is not currently applicable.
  --/| For example, the built-in Prone Roll Bonus exists while Prone is inactive.
  --/|
  --/| .135 follows the complete parent chain when reconstructing numeric totals.
  --/| It excludes explicitly disabled records, inactive Conditions/Effects,
  --/| unattuned Attunements, and descendants that require an unequipped Item.
  --/|
  --/| The compact probe below shows the IMMEDIATE parent and the most useful state
  --/| field on common parent types. It is a discovery aid, not a replacement for
  --/| ScriptCards' complete ancestry/applicability check.
  --/|
  --/| This tutorial is a discovery/diagnostic card. It does not change the sheet.
  --/| ==========================================================================

  --#beaconsheet|1
  --#sourcetoken|@{selected|token_id}
  --#title|[*S:character_name] - Roll Mode and Roll Bonus Tutorial

  --+|[c][b]Global Sheet Roll Settings[/b][/c]

  --+Global d20 Roll Mode|[*S:sheet->settings->rolls->mode]
  --+Roll Privacy|[*S:sheet->settings->rolls->privacy]
  --+Automatic Damage|[*S:sheet->settings->rollDamageAutomatic]

  --+|[c][b]Targeted Roll Bonuses[/b][/c]

  --/| The loop prints one readable line per Roll Bonus instead of dumping every
  --/| raw field. Inactive sources remain visible so you can see what WOULD apply
  --/| if that source became active.
  --%Index|0;99;1
    --&RecordName|[*S:rollbonuses->[&Index]->name]
    --?"[&RecordName]" -eq "undefined"|%!

    --/| Keep the complete stored category/target arrays so the probe cannot hide
    --/| a third or later entry. The entire record is still printed on one line.
    --&Category|[*S:rollbonuses->[&Index]->bonusCategory]
    --&Target|[*S:rollbonuses->[&Index]->bonusName]

    --&Effect|[*S:rollbonuses->[&Index]->bonusDetails]
    --&BonusValue|[*S:rollbonuses->[&Index]->bonusValue]
    --?"[&Effect]" -eq "Keep Highest"|[
      --&Effect|Advantage
    --]|
    --?"[&Effect]" -eq "Keep Lowest"|[
      --&Effect|Disadvantage
    --]|
    --?"[&Effect]" -eq "Modifier"|[
      --&Effect|Modifier [&BonusValue]
    --]|

    --&ParentID|[*S:rollbonuses->[&Index]->parentID]
    --&SourceType|[*S:sheet->integrants->integrants->[&ParentID]->type]
    --&SourceName|[*S:sheet->integrants->integrants->[&ParentID]->name]
    --&SourceState|enabled=[*S:sheet->integrants->integrants->[&ParentID]->_enabled]

    --?"[&SourceType]" -eq "Condition"|[
      --&SourceState|active=[*S:sheet->integrants->integrants->[&ParentID]->_active]
    --]|
    --?"[&SourceType]" -eq "Item"|[
      --&SourceState|equipped=[*S:sheet->integrants->integrants->[&ParentID]->equipData->equipped]
    --]|
    --?"[&SourceType]" -eq "Effect"|[
      --&SourceState|active=[*S:sheet->integrants->integrants->[&ParentID]->_active]
    --]|
    --?"[&SourceType]" -eq "Attunement"|[
      --&SourceState|attuned=[*S:sheet->integrants->integrants->[&ParentID]->_attuned]
    --]|

    --+|[b][&RecordName][/b] — category [&Category] — target [&Target] — [&Effect] — immediate parent [&SourceType]: [&SourceName] ([&SourceState])
  --%|

  --+|[c][b]What to Remember[/b][/c]

  --+Global Mode|sheet->settings->rolls->mode affects the character's general d20 mode.
  --+Targeted Overrides|Inspect rollbonuses when one skill, save, attack, or check is being modified by another rule.
  --+Source State|A Roll Bonus record can exist while its parent Condition, Effect, Attunement, or Item is not currently applicable.
  --+No Single Stealth Setting|The final effective state can be the combination of the global mode plus several applicable Roll Bonus records.
}}
